<title>NETHERLANDS: Aegon shares up on Providian deal.</title>
<headline>Aegon shares up on Providian deal.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Dutch insurer Aegon NV rose 6.80 guilders to 106.00 in early trade on Monday after the company announced it would acquire the insurance activities of Providian Corp of the United States for $3.5 billion.</p>
<p>Under the deal, expected to be finalised in early 1997, Providian Corp shareholders will receive Aegon shares worth $2.62 billion and Aegon USA will take over loans worth some $780 million and preferred stock worth $100 million.</p>
<p>The jump in Aegon stock boosted an otherwise quiet but firm Amsterdam bourse.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
